    "description": "Technical authentication, stage-support, runtime-resource, and outcome-blind retention review.",
    "generatedAt": "2026-08-02T18:43:18.107Z",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "title",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "# Prompt 12 combination pilot retention review"
      },
      {
        "id": "technical-summary",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## All four methods are operationally eligible, but no approval has been given\n\nThe pilot re-authenticates at **24/24 evaluation cells**, **18/18 unique selector fits**, and **168/168 active files**. No active cell is missing, partial, failed, timed out, interrupted, duplicated, unexpected, or hash-invalid. The outcome-blind recommendation is to retain all four preregistered methods. This report is not user approval: the approval lock is absent and DEV and OOT remain closed.",
        "sourceId": "authentication"
      },
      {
        "id": "authentication-finding",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## The live completion boundary supersedes the historical interrupt\n\nCell 001's latest state is completed and authenticated; its archived manual interrupt remains historical. The final Cell 024 completed at final_prediction with worker exit 0, no stop or error, and authentication SHA-256 8701e61330498c79e7cb9befd39d17568c5173d2433160457594b559bb230f02. No experiment worker, orphan, execution lock, stale lock, or partial file remains. Conventional manifest, checkpoint, and success-marker files are intentionally not part of this pilot's completion contract.",
        "sourceId": "authentication"
      },
      {
        "id": "authentication-table-block",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "authentication-table"
      },
      {
        "id": "support-finding",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Stage support passes with two protocol-declared natural-support bounds\n\nSixteen selection identities completed their requested or natural support directly. The Home Credit CatBoost branches for both Boruta-first refiners requested 40 features but correctly retained the 26 confirmed features, emitted infeasible_natural_support, and did not pad. Those are valid completed states that require a visible support-mismatch label, not method failures.",
        "sourceId": "stage-support"
      },
      {
        "id": "support-table-block",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "stage-support-table"
      },
      {
        "id": "runtime-finding",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Every latest-session work unit cleared runtime and resource controls\n\nAll 42 supervised work units completed with exit 0, no stop, and no supervisor resource warning. The highest process-tree RSS was 6.984 GiB versus 24 GiB warning and 28 GiB abort thresholds. The lowest system-available RAM was 22.201 GiB, 14.201 GiB above the 8 GiB abort floor. The largest observed wall-limit fraction was 1.6324%.",
        "sourceId": "runtime-review"
      },
      {
        "id": "runtime-chart-block",
        "type": "chart",
        "chartId": "selector-rss-chart"
      },
      {
        "id": "runtime-table-block",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "runtime-table"
      },
      {
        "id": "scope-definitions",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Scope and decision definitions\n\nThe review covers authenticated DEV-fold-1 pilot artifacts only. completed means the declared selection path published a valid terminal artifact. infeasible_natural_support means stage-one Boruta support was below the requested fixed budget, so the protocol forbade padding and refinement. Retention eligibility is based only on authentication, declared support behavior, and runtime-resource evidence. Predictive outcomes were not extracted, ranked, compared, or used for retention."
      },
      {
        "id": "methodology",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Authentication and aggregation method\n\nThe runner's safe status validator recomputed canonical artifact authentication, checked identity and terminal state, and verified every referenced file's size and SHA-256 without resolving raw dataset paths or starting workers. A deterministic active-tree digest independently reconciled all 168 files. Selection support came from the 18 authenticated selection checkpoints. Runtime maxima and minima came from authenticated supervisor fields and the latest successful session's finalization events."
      },
      {
        "id": "limitations",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## One fold does not guarantee later-fold cost or support\n\nThe pilot establishes operability, not constant scaling. Expanding DEV folds may realize different Boruta support and higher resource use. Natural-support mismatches must remain labelled, and DEV must preserve sequential execution, thread caps, monitoring, wall limits, warning thresholds, and abort floors. No predictive claim or method ranking is made here."
      },
      {
        "id": "retention-finding",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Retain the complete frozen method set\n\nNo method failed an admissible gate, so the recommendation is to retain all four methods in the exact runner order. This preserves the registered comparison families and avoids outcome-driven attrition. With all four retained, full DEV contains 120 evaluation cells backed by 90 selector fits across five folds.",
        "sourceId": "retention"
      },
      {
        "id": "retention-table-block",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "retention-table"
      },
      {
        "id": "next-step",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Explicit digest-and-scope approval is the only next step\n\nThe user must approve the committed review digest and exact four-method scope in a later message. Until that happens, do not create pilot_approval_lock.json, do not run or resume the pilot, do not start DEV, and do not access OOT."
      },
      {
        "id": "further-question",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Decision requested\n\nDoes the user approve the identified review digest and the proposed retained method IDs exactly as ordered in this report?"
      }
    ],
